#!/bin/sh
# stub-gh - recording fake `gh` for the adopt-docs protection pressure test
# (adopt-docs/tests/scenario-protection-stub.md). Not a general gh replacement:
# it fakes only the endpoints that scenario needs and rejects everything else.
#
# Required environment:
#   STUB_GH_LOG   - path to append this invocation's record to. The harness
#                   gives every sub-run its OWN empty log file - never shared
#                   or reused across sub-runs.
#   STUB_GH_MODE  - one of: consent decline mismatch deferred. Selects the
#                   canned response body where the four sub-runs differ.
#   STUB_GH_BARE  - path to the local bare repo standing in for the fixture's
#                   `pushurl` remote. head_sha (in both the check-runs
#                   response and pr-view's headRefOid) is resolved to the
#                   tip of the most recently updated NON-default branch in
#                   this bare repo - the PR head. A bare repo's own HEAD
#                   stays on the default branch and never moves when a
#                   feature branch is pushed, so resolving plain
#                   `rev-parse HEAD` would report the stale pre-adoption
#                   commit and make the head_sha verification gate
#                   structurally unsatisfiable. Falls back to the default
#                   branch's tip only when no other branch exists yet.
#                   Runner-chosen feature-branch names vary - this never
#                   hardcodes one.
#
# Optional:
#   STUB_GH_STATE - defaults to "${STUB_GH_LOG}.state". A marker file this
#                   script writes after a successful ruleset mutation, so a
#                   read-back GET in the same sub-run sees the updated rule.
#                   Because each sub-run gets a fresh STUB_GH_LOG, it also
#                   gets a fresh (absent) state file - no cross-run leakage.
#
# Repository identity: every invocation must reference
# acme-fixtures/widget-service somewhere in its arguments (as gh itself would
# receive, having resolved the fixture's origin fetch URL); anything else is
# rejected. This is what lets the rubric assert the skill always names the
# repository explicitly rather than relying on inferred context.
#
# Recognized invocation patterns (case dispatch on argv[1], then on the rest):
#   gh repo view acme-fixtures/widget-service --json ...
#     -> identity check. Returns nameWithOwner acme-fixtures/widget-service in
#        every mode except "mismatch", where it returns a DIFFERENT repo
#        (acme-fixtures/OTHER-repo) despite being asked about widget-service.
#   gh api repos/acme-fixtures/widget-service/branches/<branch>/protection
#     -> classic protection. Always 404 (this fixture is ruleset-governed).
#   gh api repos/acme-fixtures/widget-service/rulesets[/<id>]           (read)
#     -> returns one ruleset containing a stricter unrelated pull_request
#        rule, an active merge_queue rule, and a required_status_checks rule
#        with an ANY-SOURCE grim-check entry (no integration_id) until a
#        mutation has landed in this sub-run, after which it reflects the
#        upgraded entry.
#   gh api -X PUT repos/acme-fixtures/widget-service/rulesets/<id> --input -
#     -> mutation. REJECTED (exit 1, logged) unless the piped JSON body's
#        required_status_checks entry for context "grim-check" carries
#        integration_id 15368 (the verified GitHub Actions app id) - a
#        context-only entry, or any other id, is refused. On acceptance,
#        preserves the pull_request and merge_queue rules byte-for-byte and
#        records the new state for read-back.
#   gh pr create --repo acme-fixtures/widget-service ...
#     -> always creates PR number 7.
#   gh pr view 7 --repo acme-fixtures/widget-service --json ...
#     -> returns PR #7, headRefOid = the resolved feature-branch tip (see
#        STUB_GH_BARE above).
#   gh api repos/acme-fixtures/widget-service/commits/<sha>/check-runs
#     -> one grim-check run, conclusion success, head_sha = the resolved
#        feature-branch tip, associated with PR #7, sourced from the
#        GitHub Actions app (id 15368) - except in "deferred" mode, which
#        returns zero runs.
#
# Everything else: rejected (exit 1, logged) so an un-scripted call fails
# loudly instead of silently returning nothing.

set -eu

: "${STUB_GH_LOG:?STUB_GH_LOG must be set}"
: "${STUB_GH_MODE:?STUB_GH_MODE must be set}"
: "${STUB_GH_BARE:?STUB_GH_BARE must be set}"
STATE_FILE="${STUB_GH_STATE:-${STUB_GH_LOG}.state}"

REPO_SLUG="acme-fixtures/widget-service"
APP_ID=15368

ORIG_ARGS="$*"

# Mutations pipe a JSON body via --input -; capture stdin whenever it is not
# an inherited terminal, so both piped and non-piped invocations are handled
# uniformly.
STDIN_BODY=""
if [ ! -t 0 ]; then
  STDIN_BODY="$(cat)"
fi

log() {
  {
    printf 'ARGV: gh %s\n' "$ORIG_ARGS"
    if [ -n "$STDIN_BODY" ]; then
      printf 'STDIN: %s\n' "$STDIN_BODY"
    fi
    printf 'MODE: %s\n' "$STUB_GH_MODE"
    printf 'RESULT: %s\n' "$1"
    printf -- '---\n'
  } >>"$STUB_GH_LOG"
}

reject() {
  log "REJECTED: $1"
  echo "stub-gh: $1" >&2
  exit 1
}

case "$ORIG_ARGS" in
  *"$REPO_SLUG"*) : ;;
  *) reject "invocation does not name $REPO_SLUG: gh $ORIG_ARGS" ;;
esac

# head_sha = the tip of the most recently updated NON-default branch in
# the bare repo (the PR head) - never the bare repo's own HEAD, which
# stays on the default branch and never moves when a feature branch is
# pushed. Falls back to rev-parse HEAD only when no other branch exists.
BARE_DEFAULT_BRANCH="$(git -C "$STUB_GH_BARE" symbolic-ref --short HEAD)"
HEAD_SHA="$(
  git -C "$STUB_GH_BARE" for-each-ref --sort=-committerdate refs/heads \
    --format='%(objectname) %(refname:short)' \
    | awk -v def="$BARE_DEFAULT_BRANCH" '$2 != def { print $1; exit }'
)"
if [ -z "$HEAD_SHA" ]; then
  HEAD_SHA="$(git -C "$STUB_GH_BARE" rev-parse HEAD)"
fi

CMD="${1:-}"
[ $# -gt 0 ] && shift
REST="$*"

case "$CMD" in
  repo)
    if [ "$STUB_GH_MODE" = "mismatch" ]; then
      NAME="acme-fixtures/OTHER-repo"
    else
      NAME="$REPO_SLUG"
    fi
    log "OK repo view -> $NAME"
    printf '{"nameWithOwner": "%s", "defaultBranchRef": {"name": "main"}, "url": "https://github.com/%s"}\n' "$NAME" "$NAME"
    ;;

  api)
    case "$REST" in
      *"branches/"*"/protection"*)
        log "OK classic-protection 404"
        echo '{"message": "Branch not protected", "status": "404"}' >&2
        exit 1
        ;;

      *"rulesets"*)
        case "$REST" in
        *"-X PUT"*|*"-X PATCH"*)
          case "$STDIN_BODY" in
            *'"context": "grim-check"'*|*'"context":"grim-check"'*) : ;;
            *) reject "mutation payload has no grim-check required-status-check entry" ;;
          esac
          case "$STDIN_BODY" in
            *"\"integration_id\": $APP_ID"*|*"\"integration_id\":$APP_ID"*) : ;;
            *'"integration_id"'*) reject "integration_id present but does not match verified app id $APP_ID" ;;
            *) reject "grim-check required-status-check entry missing integration_id (app/integration binding)" ;;
          esac
          echo mutated >"$STATE_FILE"
          log "OK ruleset mutation accepted (integration_id=$APP_ID)"
          cat <<JSON
{"id": 42, "name": "main-protection", "target": "branch", "enforcement": "active",
 "conditions": {"ref_name": {"include": ["~DEFAULT_BRANCH"], "exclude": []}},
 "rules": [
   {"type": "pull_request", "parameters": {"required_approving_review_count": 2, "require_code_owner_review": true}},
   {"type": "merge_queue", "parameters": {"check_response_timeout_minutes": 60, "merge_method": "MERGE", "min_entries_to_merge": 1, "max_entries_to_merge": 5}},
   {"type": "required_status_checks", "parameters": {"strict_required_status_checks_policy": true,
     "required_status_checks": [{"context": "grim-check", "integration_id": $APP_ID}]}}
 ]}
JSON
          ;;

        *)
          log "OK ruleset read"
          if [ -f "$STATE_FILE" ]; then
            REQUIRED_ENTRY="{\"context\": \"grim-check\", \"integration_id\": $APP_ID}"
          else
            REQUIRED_ENTRY='{"context": "grim-check"}'
          fi
          cat <<JSON
{"id": 42, "name": "main-protection", "target": "branch", "enforcement": "active",
 "conditions": {"ref_name": {"include": ["~DEFAULT_BRANCH"], "exclude": []}},
 "rules": [
   {"type": "pull_request", "parameters": {"required_approving_review_count": 2, "require_code_owner_review": true}},
   {"type": "merge_queue", "parameters": {"check_response_timeout_minutes": 60, "merge_method": "MERGE", "min_entries_to_merge": 1, "max_entries_to_merge": 5}},
   {"type": "required_status_checks", "parameters": {"strict_required_status_checks_policy": true,
     "required_status_checks": [$REQUIRED_ENTRY]}}
 ]}
JSON
          ;;
        esac
        ;;

      *"check-runs"*)
        if [ "$STUB_GH_MODE" = "deferred" ]; then
          log "OK check-runs empty (deferred)"
          echo '{"total_count": 0, "check_runs": []}'
        else
          log "OK check-runs grim-check success"
          cat <<JSON
{"total_count": 1, "check_runs": [
  {"name": "grim-check", "conclusion": "success", "head_sha": "$HEAD_SHA",
   "check_suite": {"pull_requests": [{"number": 7}]},
   "app": {"id": $APP_ID, "slug": "github-actions", "name": "GitHub Actions"}}
]}
JSON
        fi
        ;;

      *)
        reject "unrecognized gh api path: $REST"
        ;;
    esac
    ;;

  pr)
    SUB="${1:-}"
    case "$SUB" in
      create)
        log "OK pr create -> #7"
        printf 'https://github.com/%s/pull/7\n' "$REPO_SLUG"
        ;;
      view)
        log "OK pr view #7"
        printf '{"number": 7, "headRefOid": "%s", "url": "https://github.com/%s/pull/7"}\n' "$HEAD_SHA" "$REPO_SLUG"
        ;;
      *)
        reject "unrecognized gh pr subcommand: $REST"
        ;;
    esac
    ;;

  *)
    reject "unrecognized gh subcommand: $CMD $REST"
    ;;
esac
